# Pokémon StreamLink — project command center

This rule guides in-session batch work. It does **not** create unattended scheduling or autonomous background execution.

## Operating limits

- Product: Pokémon StreamLink. Feature names stay short (Play, My PC, Admin Hub).
- Architecture stays static HTML + vanilla JS + `play.css` + `playCall`. No React/Tailwind.
- Do not merge to `main` or deploy. Do not stamp production APP (`20261008-rc133` until owner says otherwise).
- No SQL migrations, grants, RLS, staff-role changes, or trainer/economy/encounter/director mutations without a new owner authorization.
- Never impersonate or mutate Sora or Twinkle. PlayTester stays nonstaff unless a separately approved, cleaned-up test.
- Do not edit `admin.html` or `js/admin-live.js`. Next-hub work stays in `admin-next.html` and its modules.
- Do not call `admin_overview` or other known write-risk admin RPCs. Inspect catalogs; do not execute write-risk RPCs to discover them.
- R1/R2 and the four recorded R18 endpoints were closed by owner-authorized CODEX-34; see current RISKS.md and LAUNCH-SECURITY-HARDENING.md. Wider security review remains open. R21 stays CLOSED unless new evidence. Final release smoke stays paused pending its bounded decision.

## Approval gates (stop and report)

- Production deploy / APP stamp / merge to `main`
- SQL, grants, RLS, staff promotion
- Any privileged write, including grants, unlinks, role edits, Oak QA
- Live staff RPC testing when PlayTester is nonstaff
- Newly discovered write paths or required schema changes
- Unclear user-facing design that would invent missing trainer data

## Reporting format

After a batch: completed · blocked · next batch · tests with STATIC / LOCAL HARNESS / REAL DOM / REAL RPC / PRODUCTION labels · branch/commit · Sora NO · Twinkle NO · PlayTester role · approvals needed.

Keep `docs/project-command-center/TASKS.md`, `TASKS.json`, and `RUN-LOG.md` current on the feature branch.
